  "term": "spandrel",
  "definition": "In evolutionary biology, a spandrel is a trait that arises as a by-product of selection acting on other features rather than being directly selected for itself. In the source packet, the human chin is discussed as a possible spandrel because its form may have emerged from other craniofacial evolutionary changes instead of as a specific adaptation.",
